assertLevel -- controls whether constructors check for well-definedness
***********************************************************************

Description
===========

This global variable controls whether the *note makeCpMackeyFunctor:
makeCpMackeyFunctor, and *note
map(CpMackeyFunctor,CpMackeyFunctor,Matrix,Matrix):
map_lpCpMackeyFunctor_cmCpMackeyFunctor_cmMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, methods check
whether the input data yields a well-defined object. If *note assertLevel:
assertLevel, is set to 0 or lower, then no checks are made, and the methods
will return a Mackey functor or homomorphism (which may be malformed)
regardless of the input data. If *note assertLevel: assertLevel, is set to 1 or
higher, then the methods will check whether the input data yields a
well-defined Mackey functor or homomorphism, and if not, they will throw an
error.

The default value is 1.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note assertLevel: assertLevel, is an *note integer:
(Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,.

