boxProduct(MackeyFunctorHomomorphism,CpMackeyFunctor) -- induced maps on box products
*************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note boxProduct: boxProduct,
  * Usage: 
        F ⊠ M
        boxProduct(F,M)
        F ** M
        M ⊠ F
        boxProduct(M,F)
        M ** F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note Mackey Functor homomorphism: MackeyFunctorHomomorphism,, 
      * M, a *note C_p Mackey Functor: CpMackeyFunctor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Mackey Functor homomorphism: MackeyFunctorHomomorphism,, the
        map induced by taking the box product of M with a morphism F.

Description
===========

A map $F\colon P\to Q$ of Mackey functors can be tesnored with a Mackey functor
$M$ to form a map $M ⊠ F\colon M ⊠ P\to M ⊠ Q$.

