TorCoh -- computes Tor of two cohomological Cp-Mackey functors
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        TorCoh(i,M,N)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * M, a *note C_p Mackey Functor: CpMackeyFunctor,, 
      * N, a *note C_p Mackey Functor: CpMackeyFunctor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note C_p Mackey Functor: CpMackeyFunctor,, the $i$th cohomological
        Tor Cp-Mackey Functor of $M$ and $N$

Description
===========

Given two cohomological *note Cp-Mackey functors: CpMackeyFunctor, $M$ and $N$,
we can compute their $i$th Tor in the category of cohomological Mackey
functors.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : N = cokernel(matrix({{3}}));                |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = makeZeroOnUnderlyingMackeyFunctor (3,N);|
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : prune TorCoh(3,M,M)                         |
|                                                 |
|o3 =                   Res : 0                   |
|     cokernel | 3 |  -----------> 0  -┐ Conj : 0 |
|                    <-----------     <┘          |
|                       Tr : 0                    |
|                                                 |
|o3 : CpMackeyFunctor                             |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use TorCoh:
===================

  * "TorCoh(ZZ,CpMackeyFunctor,CpMackeyFunctor)"

